      "contraejemplo": "Entreno 134 filas al 14-01. Sin cambiar capturas, convierto el derecho de 10 TWD en ambiguo, o cambio el cierre del 12-01 de 100 a 200. Al entrenar el 21-01 no hay ValueError y permanece el manifiesto con data=fffc0aaf5753ac27. Reemplazar el calendario por otro con cierre el 12-01 y la misma versi├│n tambi├⌐n reutiliza filas. Con versi├│n de calendario nueva s├¡ se reconstruyen: ese control pasa, aunque MarketData.data_version tampoco cambia. Refuta el informe 20 ┬º2 P5 y ┬º3.2.",
      "comando_reproduccion": "python -B -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider review/out/astra_scratch/test_r15_attacks.py -k market_mutation_without --basetemp=review/out/astra_scratch/repro15_market",
      "prueba_propuesta": "from dataclasses import replace\nfrom review.out.astra_scratch.r10_support import fixture, date, time, taipei\nfrom review.out.astra_scratch.test_r13_attacks import cash\nfrom twlab.backtest import TabularForecaster\n\ndef test_changed_right_cannot_reuse_training(tmp_path):\n    _, market = fixture(tmp_path, end='2024-01-12', dividends=[cash(10)])\n    f = TabularForecaster(market, min_weeks=1, retrain_every_weeks=1)\n    f.maybe_train(taipei(date(2024,1,14), time(18)))\n    previous = f.model.training_manifest_id\n    security = next(iter(market.securities.values()))\n    security.events[0] = replace(security.events[0], ambiguous=True)\n    try:\n        f.maybe_train(taipei(date(2024,1,21), time(18)))\n    except ValueError:\n        return\n    assert f.model.training_manifest_id != previous\n",
